3.0.1 (2026-10-05)
- `use_composer` now pre-checks that composer is installed and that
  composer.json exists in the project root, aborting with a fitting error
  otherwise (TODO 2.2)

3.0.0 (2026-10-05)
- Config section restructured: the config variables now live in a single
  block between `# CONFIG START` and `# CONFIG END` markers, followed by
  per-variable documentation; ships with a placeholder host that must be
  replaced before running
- The updater now copies the user CONFIG block wholesale onto the newest
  version (no per-line parsing); both files must use the CONFIG markers
- Unconfigured placeholder hosts and incomplete host entries now abort
  with a fitting error message instead of warning or failing cryptically
- Breaking: updater no longer supports configs without the CONFIG markers

2.10.0 (2026-10-05)
- The updater replaces the user config variables in place in the downloaded
  file, keeping the new version comments and examples intact
- First-deploy dirty-repo check now runs before composer swaps to production,
  so an abort no longer leaves the local dev environment in production state

2.9.0 (2026-10-05)
- Adopted semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH); entries below use the old
  two-number format
- The updater now compares versions numerically: '2.8' and '2.8.0' are treated
  as equal, downgrades are refused, and unparseable versions are rejected

2.8.0 (2026-10-05)
- Merged upstream changes: lazy-mode commit messages (no quotation marks
  needed around the message), updated README, comments, and changelog
- Fixed lazy-mode commit messages no longer wrapped in literal quote
  characters (`commit_msg="$*"` instead of `commit_msg="'$*'"`)

2.7 (2026-10-05)
- New: `comploy --update` (or `-u`) downloads the latest comploy from its
  repository and replaces this file, porting the user config (hosts,
  ignored_files, key, use_git, use_composer, post_deployment_commands) onto
  the new version. The previous version is kept as comploy.bak.
- The download source can be overridden with the COMPLOY_UPDATE_URL
  environment variable (for mirrors or local testing).

2.6 (2026-10-05)
- Validate host config before any sync; skip or abort on empty/invalid host or
  server_dir entries, refuse to sync to the filesystem root. Prevents the
  empty default `hosts['']=''` entry from letting `rsync --delete` wipe a
  server home directory.
- Added `set -euo pipefail` so failing ssh/rsync/composer/git commands stop
  execution instead of silently continuing and reporting success.

2.6 (2025-05-05)
- Added lazy-mode for commit messages; no need to enclose the commit message in quotation marks

2.5 (2022-06-28)
- Change directory to comploy on execution, making it possible to execute it from wherever

2.4 (2022-03-30)
- On deployment, Composer now makes sure that the autoloader is optimized and that dev-packages are left out
- It is now possible to execute custom serverside commands after deployment

2.3 (2022-03-12)
- rsync now uses the `--delay-updates` option to ensure better atomicity on deployment server.

2.2 (2022-03-11)
- Composer now uses the `--optimize-autoloader` option when installing packages on the server.

2.1 (2022-03-11)
- Ignore .git folder if using git.

2.0 (2022-03-10)
- First documented version.
- Added support for Composer, comploy now auto-installs packages on execution.
- Fixed bash conditionals.
- Now uses the deployment folder for permission setup.
